; The desk: everything the risk kernel refuses to be.
;
; This library depends on ohcamel, and nothing in lib/ may depend on it. dune
; enforces the direction -- naming ohcamel_desk in lib/dune would be a cycle
; and the build would refuse it -- and CI greps lib/ for the trading host, the
; orders path and Sqlite3, because a cycle catches a dependency and not a
; pasted string. That boundary is invariant 6 now: the kernel cannot place an
; order because it cannot name anything that does.

(library
 (name ohcamel_desk)
 ; websocket and websocket-async: the trade_updates stream, framed by the
 ; libraries lib/dune lists for the market-data stream and opened over that
 ; client's TLS connection.
 (libraries
  ohcamel
  core
  async
  cohttp
  cohttp-async
  uri
  sqlite3
  yojson
  websocket
  websocket-async)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_jane))
 ; Coverage instrumentation, declared as lib/dune declares it: OFF unless dune
 ; is invoked with --instrument-with bisect_ppx, which only `make coverage` and
 ; CI's coverage job do. Without it the published figure was the kernel's
 ; alone and said nothing about the code that writes the journal and sends
 ; orders.
 (instrumentation
  (backend bisect_ppx)))
